\title{responses.build: A Workflow for Harmonising Physiological Response-Curve Data into a Documented Standard Structure}
\description{
The `responses.build` package provides a workflow to harmonise physiological response-curve data - leaf gas exchange, hydraulic vulnerability, and fluorescence response curves - from diverse sources into a documented, relational structure. It is a fork of `traits.build` (Wenk et al, 2024, \doi{10.1016/j.ecoinf.2024.102773}, \url{https://github.com/traitecoevo/traits.build}), which harmonises single-valued trait data; this package extends the same data model to measurements that form curves, where a response is measured across a driver gradient and the individual points belong to an identifiable curve. It was built to support AusFizz (\url{https://github.com/traitecoevo/ausfizz}). For the shared data model and workflow concepts see \url{https://traitecoevo.github.io/traits.build-book/}.
}
